+*stop_state*:: '(returns integer)' -
+  current resumable Stop state. One of `STOP_IDLE`, `STOP_STOPPING`,
+  `STOP_STOPPED`, `STOP_STARTING`.
+
+*hold_wait*:: '(returns integer)' -
+  while a Stop is `STOP_STOPPING` or the program is paused, the operation the
+  hold waits for before the machine holds. An operation already handed to
+  another subsystem runs to its end first, and Abort is the way out. One of
+  `HOLD_WAIT_NONE`, `HOLD_WAIT_HOMING` (a queued `G28.2`), `HOLD_WAIT_IO` (a
+  tool change or other I/O command), `HOLD_WAIT_SYSTEM_COMMAND` (a user
+  `M100`-`M199` program).
+
 *interpreter_errcode*:: '(returns integer)' -
   current RS274NGC interpreter return code. One of
   INTERP_OK, INTERP_EXIT, INTERP_EXECUTE_FINISH, INTERP_ENDFILE,
@@ -640,6 +652,14 @@ c.tool_offset(toolno, z_offset,  x_offset, diameter, frontangle, backangle, orie
 `abort()`::
   send EMC_TASK_ABORT message.
 
+`program_stop()`::
+  stop an active AUTO program without clearing its interpreter or motion
+  queues. The program can be continued with Run, Resume, or Single Step.
+  Position-synchronized motion (`G33`, `G33.1`) and a queued `G28.2` homing
+  cycle run to completion before the program holds.
+  The command is rejected when no AUTO program is active; use `abort()` when
+  execution must be terminated.
+
 `auto(int[, int])`::
   run, step, pause or resume a program.
 
